FUTURE ISSUES
1. What are the origins and characteristics of the individual complex trajectories and chaotic-like dynamics of isolated droplets observed in experiments?
2. How can we model the dynamics of many active droplets or within complex geometries, while retaining the intrinsic nonlinearity of the hydrochemical coupling? Are direct numerical simulations the only resort? If so, what are the most adapted methods to accurately treat the nonlinear coupling and moving droplet boundaries?
3. What is the influence of active droplets’ geometric environment on their motion? How relevant are bulk models for understanding observations?
4. Existing models place much focus on hydrodynamic and transport modeling. Are the details of the physical chemistry involved important? What are the role and features of the surfactant dynamics at the densely covered interface?
5. Can the motion of active droplets be controlled? If so, how and for which purposes can they realistically be used for engineering applications?
